          "filename": "American Trust Building, 3rd Avenue and Union Street, Nashville, TN (54385292423).jpg",
          "caption": "Built in 1926, this Classical Revival-style building was designed by Henry C. Hibbs for the American Trust Company to serve as the headquarters of the bank.  The building is clad in limestone and marbled with fluted doric pilasters and engaged columns flanking window bays with metal spandrels a the lower portion of the building, one-over-one windows, a cornice with dentils and modillions, a granite base, and corinthian pilasters on the upper section of the building.   The building is a contributing structure in the Nashville Financial Historic District, listed on the National Register of Historic Places in 2002.  The building today serves as part of the Hotel Indigo Countrypolitan.",
